ffmpeg in the server image (server/Dockerfile)
----------------------------------------------

The image installs Debian 13's own packages for the quality levels
(server/src/levels/), from deb.debian.org:

  ffmpeg (7.1.x)  FFmpeg built by Debian with --enable-gpl, linking libx264
                  and libx265, so FFmpeg itself is under the GNU General Public
                  License, version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later). Debian's main
                  section holds only free software: the build links no non-free
                  codec (no libfdk-aac), so the image may be redistributed.
  intel-media-va-driver-non-free
                  Intel Media Driver for VAAPI (iHD), MIT (Expat), parts
                  BSD-3-Clause. Debian files it under non-free only because its
                  GPU kernels ship as prebuilt binaries; it is redistributable.
  libmfx-gen1.2, libvpl2
                  The oneVPL GPU runtime and dispatcher, MIT.
  libva, libdrm   MIT. The remaining libraries ffmpeg pulls in (codecs, filters,
                  fonts) are each under their own free licence.

Each package's copyright file is in the image at
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. The corresponding source of every package
is Debian's source package of the installed version: `apt-get source <package>`,
https://sources.debian.org or https://snapshot.debian.org (dpkg -l in the image
lists the versions).

ffmpeg and ffprobe run as separate processes, spawned by the server
(server/src/levels/encoder.ts, server/src/levels/backend-check.ts) and fed
through pipes and command-line arguments. The server neither links nor bundles
any of their code, so its own licence (LGPL-2.1-or-later, above) is unaffected.

WebRTC (server/src/rtc/)
------------------------

The server bundles werift 0.25.1 (https://github.com/shinyoshiaki/werift-webrtc), a
WebRTC implementation in TypeScript, and the packages it uses, into
server/dist/server.mjs. server/src/rtc/udp-mux.ts wraps werift's UdpTransport.init
so that every peer connection shares one UDP port; it contains no werift code.

